A||||1||Mach10||I'm back from my trip!||||14||
Z||000000||Mach10||08-11-2001||02:42 AM||||Just got back from a lovely 2-week holiday on the west coast of Canada. I've learned a few things:<BR>1) My Fiero *IS* reliable enough to travel 2400km each way<BR>2) With some creativity, it is possible to pack my car with a staggering amount of baggage/supplies.<BR>3) Gas mileage is pretty good, even with a v-6 behind me<BR>4) I have sufficient range to get between gas stations even out in the boonies<BR>5) The seats are more than comfortable, even on long journeys. I didn't even get a hint of the sore back that I'd get in any other car!<BR>6) Passing can be fun<BR>7) Alberta drivers are terrible. <BR>8) Alberta ricers are worse<BR>9) Semi trucks are your friend if you let them in on merge-lanes<BR>10) RVs belong in hell, or alternatively, on any other road other than the one I am on.<BR>11) For some reason, long-distance pickup-truck drivers are invariably assholes (please feel free to prove me wrong. PLEASE!)<BR>12) 6-cyls are great in the mountains. I can still speed up. Every 4-cyl I met couldn't and would slow down on steep grades. I was able to maintain speed, and even pass with ease.<P>A very informative journey. And relaxing. Of course, I come home to a complete fiasco of Fiero-related business. A couple of missing MOs, a customs screw-up, and another customs screw-up. It's going to be fun sorting THIS mess out.||||reg||14
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||08-11-2001||08:34 AM||||Sounds like you had a good time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I like how you wrote <B>2) With some creativity, it is possible to pack my car with a staggering amount of baggage/supplies.</B>   Your not kidding, I learned that when I went down to Carlisle.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
